meta {
  name: Start Application (Student)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/application-forms/{{admissionCycleId}}/application
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "nationality": "Indian",
    "course_id": "{{courseId}}",
    "state_of_domicile": "Karnataka",
    "passport_country": null,
    "passport_number": null,
    "campus_id": null
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data && data.data.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("applicationId", data.data.id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Creates a NEW draft Application for the authenticated student against
  this admission cycle (404 if the cycle doesn't exist, 409 if it's not
  currently "open", 409 if today is before the cycle's startsOn date, 409
  if today is after its endsOn deadline — inclusive of the whole endsOn
  day). NOT idempotent anymore: a student can have several separate
  Applications under the same cycle now (one per course) — this always
  creates a new Application row, 409 only if the requested course_id is
  already actively (non-withdrawn) selected in ANY of the student's
  existing applications AT THIS COLLEGE — across every admission cycle,
  not just this one.

  The deadline is checked ONLY here, at Start — once an Application has
  been started, the student can keep filling it in, paying, and
  submitting even if the cycle's endsOn date passes afterward. It never
  blocks an already-started draft, only a brand-new one.

  `nationality` is required and drives NRI-style application-fee surcharges
  applied on the primary course's fee. `course_id` is REQUIRED — this
  becomes the application's primary course, and its fee is what payment
  gates before the rest of the flow (details, documents, declaration,
  submit) unlocks. No quota is set here — the primary course starts
  quota-less, same as every other course; use Change Application Course
  Quota afterward if a quota applies. `state_of_domicile` /
  `passport_country` / `passport_number` are optional, relevant mainly for
  foreign-nationality applicants. `campus_id` is optional and must belong
  to the cycle's college if given.

  Typical next steps: browse List Course Catalogue (courses + their quota
  options in one call) to add more courses or pick a quota via Change
  Application Course Quota, then POST
  /payments/applications/{{applicationId}}/initiate to pay — nothing else
  on the application unlocks until that payment is confirmed.
}
